From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Reinsmidt <735251+ericreinsmidt@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] squashfs with LZ4, for a read-only root that reads less off the
 card: the boot is held back by the card from the root mount to TortOS's first
 frame, and an LZ4 squashfs image is about half the bytes, with the boot's
 files packed together in the order it reads them. One decompressor per CPU,
 as several programs read the root at once while the Brick boots; no zlib,
 which the image doesn't use

---
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/brick_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/brick_defconfig
@@ -261,6 +261,10 @@
 # CONFIG_PROC_PAGE_MONITOR is not set
 CONFIG_TMPFS=y
 CONFIG_TMPFS_POSIX_ACL=y
+CONFIG_SQUASHFS=y
+CONFIG_SQUASHFS_DECOMP_MULTI_PERCPU=y
+# CONFIG_SQUASHFS_ZLIB is not set
+CONFIG_SQUASHFS_LZ4=y
 CONFIG_PSTORE=y
 # CONFIG_PSTORE_DEFLATE_COMPRESS is not set
 CONFIG_PSTORE_BLK=y
